 "links": {
  "about": "The one https-link rule every pairing's link check uses: the raw string holds no whitespace (Unicode White_Space), control character (Unicode Cc) or backslash; it parses as an absolute URL; its scheme is https, compared case-insensitively (RFC 3986 §3.1); it has a host, a DNS name (RFC 1123 labels) or an IP literal (RFC 3986 §3.2.2), and no userinfo (RFC 3986 §3.2.1). Each row gives the link and whether the rule accepts it. 'refusedAs' is what a pairing's placement and reading give the same value as the legalContextUrl and as the agreement URL, alike, so that one value has one meaning everywhere: link-not-https only for a string of at most 2048 characters that parses as an absolute URL whose scheme is not https, and legal-context-malformed for every other value the rule refuses (not a string, empty, unparseable, no host, over 2048 characters, or an https URL the rule refuses).",
